1784192304584388	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx9As		item.comment	bn-3hch	{"body":"Read-only source/protocol integration audit complete; workspace remains clean at 8b40d1bb and no Rust build, test, measurement, or evidence generation ran. Authority checked: full BN-2L3N-PROTOCOL v3; Asterism benchmark/formal/authority/review/spike research; merged overlay producer/source; runner 40a743a3 in bn-11dt; evaluator/schema/terminal 4e4f44d0 in bn-2asn; current store/log APIs and tests. Dependency state is correct: bn-yh11 done, bn-3hch doing, bn-znj5 blocked on this integration.\n\nAcceptance map: (1) Common oracle core exists in overlay/public/main.rs for EventStore<FjallSnapshotBackend<LogEngine>> with generation adapters, but the exact runner schedules it only for C/D; A must execute the same semantic core inside frozen current-product case public-ordinary-append-command-cache-read-subscribe, plus current command/cache coverage. Critical blocker: correctness_oracle currently never connects to Control, while runner run_child(controlled=True) requires boot/runtime/opened/ready/start/measured/release; C/D oracle would fail/hang. (2) Normalized accounting is substantially present: visible records, versions, payload/type, outcomes, heads and opaque cursor order are generation-neutral; current/D separately assert v3 registry gaps and C asserts no metadata positions. Never renumber current positions. (3) Current source tests already cover ordinary facade, exact race, registry ordering/rejection/error precedence, borrowed/owned parity, cancellation-after-ownership, live rolls, repeated/active/sealed recovery, scanner/torn cases, sidecar fallback, committer poison and reservation bounds. They are not yet integrated into the two exact prebuilt ast-rb-check / ast-rb-fault children or their exact 27-case output. Missing public child coverage is strongest for deterministic cancel-before-admission, five kill phases, public-composition short/write/fdatasync injection, semantic corrupt-registry mutation, and compile-out attestation. (4) Only existing deterministic engine seam is TestOwnerCohortGate in engine.rs under cfg(test); there are no named pre-write, post-write/pre-barrier, post-barrier/pre-publication, or post-publication/pre-completion hooks. LogEngine hardcodes RealRuntime, while SimFs fault coverage is low-level. A normal example/integration test compiles mess-store as a non-test dependency, so cfg(test) hooks are unavailable; the correctness-tool build architecture must explicitly compile a separately materialized current library/harness with cfg(test), never a feature or release-path hook. (5) Runner/overlay already seed 2M domain events at 1000 streams x 200 batches x 10, 64 B, 8 MiB, Process; verify/close, hash, make archive read-only, materialize a fresh byte-identical copy, syncfs, and quiet-guard each child. Critical blocker: seed emits 16-hex FNV logical/head digests but exact runner smoke and seed validation require 64 lowercase hex, so reopen is not currently runnable. (6) Exact Latin A-C-D/C-D-A/D-A-C rows and separate fresh-copy A/C/D structural reopen traces already exist; evaluator independently enforces copy identity, 2M count, order, handshake monotonicity, and discarded trace wall.\n\nMinimal no-schema-drift plan: keep runner/evaluator schemas untouched; add shared controlled-correctness/oracle source used byte-identically by C/D and A case 1; fix shared digest serialization to the exact 64-hex contract; build current ast-rb-check with exact seven current-product cases and ast-rb-fault with exact twenty current-fault cases/order/boundedness; add narrowly named cfg(test)-only admission/write/barrier/publication/completion seams and real-process self-exec kill workers, with test-only real-FS syscall injection; use close/mutate/reopen for torn/CRC/registry/sidecar gates; add a source-approved pre-approval tool-build/attestation stage that records exact source/patch/toolchain and compares a hook-overlay release A binary byte-for-byte with the pristine unhooked build, plus symbol/string absence, embedding the attestation consumed by case 27. Likely files: tooling/overlay/public/main.rs, shared control/digest and a new shared semantic-oracle module, new current correctness/fault harness sources and test-only overlay patch inputs, prepare_overlays.py/README/source-plan allowlists and static self-tests; avoid changes to evidence_schema.py, runner, evaluator, or terminal.\n\nStatic checks available before product builds: exact case/group/argv/env/schema mapping, source allowlists, every hook syntactically cfg(test)-guarded, no runner/evaluator drift, overlay self-test assertions, and clean diffs. Product builds are required later for hooked-child compilation, release byte identity and symbol absence proof, exact child transition smokes, public fault/reopen behavior, and only after bn-znj5 review/lease for 2M corpus or measurement evidence."}	blake3:jIqRp45B46dRorpL-wN0-uW8sogO0TpS_ygvK9vdwTw
1784192954190269	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx9Qs		item.comment	bn-3hch	{"body":"First bounded integration slice committed in workspace bn-3hch: 53845bd655642c865037fed1459d3023e0622120, tree eaf10752c7f44811ddea81d8b307af99248196b6. The common C/D correctness oracle now uses the existing shared Control API for the exact ordinary-child boot -> runtime -> opened -> ready/start -> measured/release sequence, including context/protocol/variant identity, chained nonces, allocator/process-CPU/monotonic counter fields, and output only after release. No runner/evaluator/schema change.\n\nReopen logical and registry/head digests retain the same dependency-free u64 FNV semantics and now use canonical left-zero-padded 64 lowercase hex via LogicalDigest::canonical_hex ({:064x}). Static authority independently mirrors the fixed A smoke seed: per-stream payload 0..63 digest 8368214f77995ee5; combined logical e2d874aa120f66af -> 000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000e2d874aa120f66af; registry stream/head (0,0) 88201fb960ff6465 -> 00000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000088201fb960ff6465. Hostile source tests reject old 16-hex output.\n\nAdded generation-specific seed accounting at the public engine surface. Exact log_events are A=3/C=1/D=3 for the specialized one-stream/one-event seed; A/D count stream registration + shared type registration + domain event, while C has no metadata positions. The full 2M corpus consequently expects A/D=2,001,001 and C=2,000,000.\n\nPermitted checks: prepare_overlays.py static-self-test PASS; exact commit git diff --check PASS; nightly rustfmt check PASS for modified digest/adapters; nightly rustfmt parse PASS for public main with injected child modules skipped. No cargo, rustc, product build/test, timing, measurement, or evidence ran. Workspace clean. Remaining bn-3hch work is the exact A seven-case correctness child, twenty-case fault child, reviewed cfg(test)-only phase/fault hooks, release absence/byte-identity proof, and later product/runner transition smokes after integration review."}	blake3:LVA6KtUyQV9gDljTMxjWkbCRhVmI5XraEOeqF97tai0
1784193055940190	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx9gs		item.comment	bn-2asn	{"body":"Remediated Seal review cr-3u5b0u HIGH thread th-3iud1l in commit 8a3d342acd70abf8d463a8001b2477e9e9e7fe23 (tree 3c1bc0a27664e2d679d6a80e512bef2ef9bbd644), atop transition-authority commit 4e4f44d04642dd834988c4d79dcb0426cd5b62f5. Specialized corpus authority now comes from stable no-follow snapshots of both exact deterministic stores actually opened by smoke_reopen and smoke_structural_reopen, tied to each child ASTERISM_REBASELINE_STORE. Both executed-copy canonical manifests must match byte/hash-for-byte/hash; the retained runner-40a source is required, exact 0555/0444, and must match the common copies. Context archive/copy digests derive only from that common executed-copy manifest. Roots and every regular-file device/inode identity are pairwise non-aliased; regular files require nlink=1. Descriptor-relative traversal opens every root component with O_NOFOLLOW, compares pre-open lstat to fstat, freezes recursive name sets/root/subdirectory identities, rechecks file and ancestor identities after reads, and rejects file/nested-ancestor/root replacement races. The exact A fixed seed is independently derived from shared/digest.rs FNV semantics: domain=1, visible=1, log=3 (stream registration + event-type registration + domain event), logical=000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000e2d874aa120f66af, registry=00000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000088201fb960ff6465. Arbitrary 64-hex, legacy 16-hex, and old log=1 coordinated raw/context/environment/provenance rebinds are rejected. This integrates with bn-3hch canonical 64-character producer rendering; schema remains v3 with no serialized field/result changes. Checks with bytecode disabled: evaluator SELF_TEST_PASS 150/150; terminal SELF_TEST_PASS 58/58; exact positive rc0 ADMIT with zero errors; just fmt-check PASS; AST 3/3; git diff --check PASS. No Seal review, build, measurement, sync, or merge performed by this worker. Pre-existing untracked Seal review directories and __pycache__ left untouched."}	blake3:rN6uGYl9ien40YK7OG7ol-oalnjwcj-V8nOjL0l0TiY
1784218887914414	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx9ws		item.comment	bn-3hch	{"body":"Approved MEDIUM cr-2l039r/th-3hmdsf static-authority remediation committed in workspace bn-3hch as 6184313bc3a6d07bbb988db1a8353bcd88ac32a3, tree 0cf8b277c0fe6a6454de009a299c36113d2616d6, on top of 53845bd655642c865037fed1459d3023e0622120. Changed only spikes/asterism_rebaseline/tooling/prepare_overlays.py; runtime overlay, shared runtime sources, schemas, runner, and evaluator are unchanged. Validators now require exact ordered shared-Control ready arguments and measured wire field/expression bindings; exact correctness-oracle ready/measured nonce, allocation, CPU, and monotonic-counter tuples; exact public seed-accounting call; exact full and smoke seed routes; and exact A/C/D high-water formulas. Static authority independently asserts full A=2,001,001 C=2,000,000 D=2,001,001 and smoke A=3 C=1 D=3. Hostiles reject allocation, CPU, ready/counter, completion/counter, and t0/t1 same-typed swaps; A/C/D domain_events + 17 formula mutations; full/smoke workload mutations; and seed accounting argument swaps. Permitted checks PASS: prepare_overlays.py static-self-test; Python AST parse; nightly rustfmt check for unchanged digest/current/borrowed adapter sources; nightly rustfmt parse for public main with children skipped; exact commit diff check. No cargo, rustc, product build/test, timing, measurement, evidence, Seal mutation, merge, or bone close ran. Remaining bn-3hch implementation is unchanged: exact A seven-case correctness child, twenty-case fault child, cfg(test)-only hooks/fault injection, release absence/byte-identity proof, and later integrated product/runner transition smokes after review."}	blake3:vIh9bQ-6fRc-W_rypPYxlSUq3zpXoxn2b1Ni375VYNQ
