1784233129121289	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExtQw		item.comment	bn-3hch	{"body":"Integration invariant (2026-07-16): source approval may bind the immutable preapproval current-children attestation, its final tools manifest, reviewed lock authority/bundle, and an exact requirement to repeat release equality under the eventual real approval. It must not try to embed the final proof hash, because that proof contains the source-approval SHA-256 and would create a cycle. After approval, build ordinary unhooked A once as the published A, build one product-test-overlay A twin with the same approved source/lock/toolchain/contract and no cfg(test)/wrapper, require byte+symbol+forbidden-string identity, record source_approval_sha256 in the final proof, and require final pristine SHA-256 == prepared variants.A.binary.sha256. Evaluator/terminal must replay the bound preapproval attestation, canonical reviewer verdict assertion, same pinned nm identity, and final proof rather than trusting free-form review_id/time."}	blake3:9M_nsD45BGm1nOMrcRD8ldPs0uIbWLcUUOC0LqlKOGI
