1784336598694727	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExjg8		item.comment	bn-znj5	{"body":"Prepared-v3-r1 root cause proven: in prepare_overlays.py the release compile-out replay reads preapproval nm authority via preapproval_nm.get('path'), but the producer RetainedFile.record() emits only {identity, path_chain, trusted_system}; the path lives at identity.path (/usr/bin/nm). str(None) yields Path('None'), resolved against the repository as .maw/workspaces/bn-znj5/None, giving the exact ENOENT from the r1 log, timestamped immediately after the proof-only A contract. Second latent defect at the same site: nm_full (flat identity dict from open_retained_artifact) is compared to the 3-key record wrapper and could never be equal even with the path fixed. Both frozen r1 bindings and live r9 attestation confirm the schema. Product-code defect: creating a bug bone, fresh workspace from exact 2bd1dcc5, narrow repair plus tests, independent review, then full r22/r23/r9/r2 lineage regeneration per handoff."}	blake3:uBRVgZ6FZrCnJS2J2V-SYgXBb4QXWpCBj1ujtW29Kks
1784336749608597	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExjw8		item.create	bn-3i0w	{"description":"The current-children producer (RetainedFile.record in tooling/current/build_children.py) emits the preapproval nm authority as {identity, path_chain, trusted_system}, with the file identity fields (path, sha256, mode, size, inode, ...) nested under identity. Four consumers instead read flat keys off the wrapper: (1) tooling/prepare_overlays.py produce_release_compile_out does Path(str(preapproval_nm.get('path'))) -> Path('None') resolved against the repository -> ENOENT .maw/workspaces/bn-znj5/None, which is the exact prepared-v3-r1 failure; it also compares open_retained_artifact's flat identity against the wrapper, which can never be equal. (2) evidence_schema.py, (3) evaluate.py, and (4) verify_terminal.py all build expected nm-tool records from flat preapproval_nm.get('mode'/'ctime_ns'/'path'/...) and would fail closed with 'preapproval nm authority is absent/differs' once a terminal attestation is validated. Repair: unwrap and strictly validate the record wrapper (same idiom as the existing dev_null wrapper validation in prepare_overlays), read identity fields from preapproval_nm['identity'], compare retained-artifact identity against the identity object, and add positive plus hostile tests covering wrapper shape, missing identity, and flat legacy shape rejection. Parent chain: part of bn-znj5 prepared-build recovery; full r22/r23/r9/r2 authority lineage must be regenerated after integration.","kind":"bug","labels":["asterism","benchmark","risk:high"],"title":"Fix preapproval nm authority schema mismatch across compile-out consumers"}	blake3:ApyIXVVztP0wGPRHMPaK4QtMDrafo3DnD0OWJt8EeNo
