1784681416377659	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx9w8		item.comment	bn-d0x6	{"body":"REBOOT INVALIDATED v5 prepared root: prepared artifacts pin /dev/null and /dev full stat identity INCLUDING changed_ns/modified_ns, which devtmpfs resets at boot. Recorded /dev/null changed_ns=1784642963633046099 vs live 1784680957652304069 (inode/device/major/minor/perms all still match). CONSTRAINT: a prepared root is only valid within the boot session it was built in -- no reboot between prepare and the run (applies to the declared run too). Relaunched full rebuild as v6 (/tmp/hoff-rebuild-v6.sh) reusing clean v5-tool-wt at 75380871, chaining the rehearsal (rehearsal-v6-r1) immediately after STEP8 so both happen in one boot."}	blake3:Lbtlr-sjI45cviolqOCwMHssi8VmJe-d2y95zK7MQKE
1784686519452788	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx-A8		item.create	bn-2304	{"description":"Found by bn-d0x6 v4 rehearsal: correctness child ast-rb-check --smoke aborts (SIGABRT, exit -6), closing its control socket and fail-stopping the run. TWO defects in crates/mess-store/src/engine.rs (cfg(test) owner-cohort scaffolding): (1) RACE: wait_until_cohort_admitted does a one-shot disarm on SUCCESS (state.armed=None + notify_all at 1331-1332) when cohort.admitted==expected. The other waiter (1292-1305) loops 'while state.armed.is_some_and(|c| c.admitted < at_least)' then asserts 'state.armed.is_some_and(|c| c.admitted >= at_least)'. A waiter woken by that success notify sees armed==None, exits the loop, and fails the assert 'owner cohort was disarmed before the requested admission' -- even though its admission succeeded. The assert conflates disarm-on-success with failure; note 1315 checks state.generation but the 1292 loop does not. (2) PANIC-IN-DROP: the assert panics while holding the MutexGuard, poisoning the mutex; unwinding drops TestOwnerCohortGuard (1354-1356) which calls disarm (1336) doing self.state.lock().expect(...) on the poisoned lock -> double panic -> SIGABRT, destroying the original diagnostic. FIX SKETCH: (a) let the waiter treat 'cleared after full admission' as success (track completion/generation that survives disarm, mirroring the generation check at 1315); (b) make disarm/Drop poison-tolerant (unwrap_or_else(|e| e.into_inner())) so a panic cannot cascade into an abort. Evidence: rehearsal-v6-r1/raw/smoke/00031.stderr, child-manifest ord=31 exit_status=-6.","kind":"bug","labels":["asterism"],"title":"mess-store owner-cohort gate: success-path disarm makes waiters assert; poisoned-lock double panic in Drop"}	blake3:gRHGItMeVr8QQ39gF26MACx1wcMEIji6H5XfIf-pGSs
1784686529411815	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx-Q8		item.comment	bn-d0x6	{"body":"REHEARSAL RESULT (rehearsal-v6-r1, 22:01:23-22:07:52): v4 pipeline VALIDATED end-to-end -- 31 children ran, 27 smoke children across ALL tracks (primary, new_names, fairness, cpu_profiles, syscall_profiles, structural_traces, reopen, correctness) x variants A/B/C/D. perf control-fd ACK framing WORKS against real pinned perf (.perf.ack = 'ack\\nack\\n' ledger entries, stderr 'Events disabled/enabled'), resolving the protocol's outstanding known defect. strace/structural traces work. O(n^2) fix confirmed (init in seconds). ONLY failure: correctness child ast-rb-check --smoke (physical ord 31) SIGABRT exit -6 from a mess-store engine.rs owner-cohort defect (see new bug bone) -> control socket closed before measured -> fail-stop. This is a PRODUCT bug in the kernel under measurement, not a harness bug. 30/31 children exited 0."}	blake3:oWLbDxnEZKKzEvd7I67prrSAw-MoqX9xeoLbb7dPEz0
