1784742771185303	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExhhA		item.comment	bn-d0x6	{"body":"PROCESS FIX + relaunch. Root cause of churn: one engine.rs change fans out into ~8 independently-pinned hashes/line-anchored patches. Fixed cascade: bn-2304 (engine), bn-1gtb (overlay patch rebase +16 x17 hunks/ordinals + ENGINE_SHA256), bn-3hlo (6 stale pins: engine c995c27d->fe559d6a in evaluate.py/verify_terminal.py/build_children.py; patch db060c90->fe53ead5 in prepare_overlays.py/profile_adapters.py/prepare_children.py). Trunk now 6913e855. NEW TOOLING (in cache, not repo, to avoid triggering rebuilds): preflight.sh runs every cheap validator in ~30s (worktree clean/at-trunk, overlay validate+self-test+git apply --check, 4 tooling self-tests, runner/verifier self-tests, timed manifest probe for O(n^2), load, disk, helpers, /dev/null identity vs prepared root for reboot-invalidation); it caught 3 failures in 30s leading to the 6 pins, saving ~6 rebuild cycles. rebuild.sh is preflight-gated with an EXIT trap emitting DRIVER-FAILED/DRIVER-END sentinels. Monitoring now two-layer: log monitor bval5wa9o + process-liveness backstop b822te3gl (fixes the 3h silent death). Launched rebuild.sh v9 at 13:52, preflight PASS. TODO after green: land preflight.sh/rebuild.sh in repo."}	blake3:V41rOWEfS89gNjtYGAXj8Na8rhUESquJMvupWbTTWO8
1784745399335591	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExhxA		item.create	bn-sqr3	{"description":"The correctness/fault children are built from a git archive of the PINNED product commit d644dc58, not trunk, so bn-2304's engine.rs fix never reached them. The cohort gate is cfg(test)-only so it is absent from the measured A/B/C/D release binaries, so there is no reason to move the variant-A pin. Revert bn-2304/bn-1gtb/bn-3hlo (restoring trunk engine.rs == pinned engine.rs, the invariant validate_product_test_overlay depends on) and deliver the same fix as 1:1 line replacements in product-test-overlay.patch, which is applied to the archived engine before building children. Overlay constraint: non-tail hunks must be exact same-size replacements. Re-land the product fix on trunk after the rebaseline.","kind":"task","labels":["asterism"],"title":"Deliver owner-cohort fix via product test overlay; revert trunk engine change"}	blake3:-eG-vCU4dwhZhHf8MaRM6n2eaC_kXvqDhDaBddxyW7g
