1784761354307258	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExjRA		item.create	bn-1csq	{"description":"RetainedSemanticManifest.verify -> _semantic_directory_identity includes st_nlink, st_size, st_mtime_ns, st_ctime_ns for every ANCESTOR DIRECTORY of a retained manifest. The runner creates its own output dir (rehearsal-*) inside .../asterism-rebaseline/, which is an ancestor of the prepared root's manifests, so that dir's nlink/mtime/ctime legitimately change mid-run and frozen_recheck fail-stops ('semantic manifest ancestor changed while retained'). Empirically confirmed: adding a subdir bumps a directory's nlink+mtime+ctime. These fields are entry-churn byproducts, not path-substitution signals; dev+ino+mode+uid+gid fully detect ancestor substitution/relink/chmod/chown. Fix: _semantic_directory_identity returns (st_dev, st_ino, st_mode, st_uid, st_gid) only. File-level manifest checks (content sha + file identity incl times) are unchanged. Found by bn-d0x6 v10 rehearsal, first run to reach frozen_recheck (correctness child now passes). cfg: this is harness code (run_rebaseline.py, embedded) so needs a rebuild.","kind":"bug","labels":["asterism"],"title":"frozen_recheck: retained-ancestor directory identity must exclude entry-churn fields"}	blake3:hqGPE_9xaZOvHdTVRldGXVEKP_sib3Y8pFUTy2tx6eQ
