1784816535209673	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExoRA		item.comment	bn-d0x6	{"body":"Profile-authority Phase-4 redundant re-validation removed (bn-3vvb) merged 1cd220ab: -5317/+247 lines; dropped the 427-line stale duplicate of evidence_schema's source-review validators (runner+evaluator still validate the chain canonically). Kept run-claim binding + profile-tool + release-compile-out authority. Fable-mapped, independently verified (test_profile_adapters 46/46, runner self-test 163/163 with edited adapter, verifier 187/187). This resolves the whole profile_adapters v4-drift class in one change instead of ~28 rebuilds. Launching v14."}	blake3:Jd4OJczpzfy77Bxj8gyTZ7FhnQO6ASg858vii0kRbzg
1784825784658561	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExohA		item.create	bn-1v5m	{"description":"profile_adapters._validate_release_compile_out_authority hardcodes expected_mode=0o555 for the release-proof nm tool, but nm is the live system /usr/bin/nm (mode 0o755, root-owned, not a write-stripped pinned child). The canonical evidence_schema validator derives the nm tool mode from the preapproval authority (release_compile_out.nm.identity.mode = 0o755). The stale 0o555 fail-stops the rehearsal with ProfileEvidenceError('release proof nm tool mode authority differs'). Fix: derive expected_mode from preapproval nm identity mode so the two validators cannot diverge.","kind":"task","title":"fix: profile_adapters nm tool mode authority derives from preapproval (bn-2l3n)"}	blake3:ObvvbdXz6KOmqehrbxD7yCIbzJlYpbippHjVZizkx-o
1784826483470089	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExoxA		item.move	bn-1v5m	{"state":"done"}	blake3:TIokZa_JnQnzvqH5iEp7QUkOyoO3dhldsmiDqgJn0P8
1784832760916055	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExpBA		item.create	bn-4gsg	{"description":"validate_profile_authority's profile-tool loop requires the runtime tool binding to fully equal BOTH the source-approved tools-manifest AND prepared.tools, including path. But prepare-build copies base tools into the prepared root, so the approved manifest records the base-tools path (bn-znj5-base-tools-*/tools/strace) while runtime/prepared use the prepared-root path (.../artifacts/tools/strace). Full-dict equality with the approved manifest is therefore impossible -> ProfileEvidenceError('profile tool strace binding differs'). The runner's own load_prepared reconciles this by comparing only (sha256, executable_mode, comm), excluding the relocatable path. Fix profile_adapters to do the same, and make the test fixture model the base->prepared relocation so it guards the bug.","kind":"task","title":"fix: profile tool binding compares identity not relocatable path (bn-2l3n)"}	blake3:xS1cUBNx--1LXsA1YGVRwTSPvv_U3NVKll4pAdIieYg
1784833147470353	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExpRA		item.move	bn-4gsg	{"state":"done"}	blake3:AGPwRbHZNpvEthvQzohH8jIHrJtTaz7-sEca0nEcC6w
1784839476715811	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExphA		item.create	bn-354w	{"description":"The first primary measurement cell panics at boot: workload.rs DurabilityKind::parse only accepts lowercase 'process'/'group', but the entire harness (run_rebaseline.py cell config, ASTERISM_DURABILITY env, evidence_schema, config.json, 32-cell identity, reporting) uses the canonical label form 'Process'/'Group' (DurabilityKind::label). parse() is the lone outlier -> panic 'durability must be process or group'. Never surfaced before because no rehearsal reached the primary cells. Fix: parse() accepts both 'Process'|'process' and 'Group'|'group', keeping the whole evidence chain consistent on 'Process'/'Group'. workload.rs is hash-pinned in overlay_pins.py, so update PINNED_SHARED_OVERLAY_SHA256.","kind":"task","title":"fix: workload DurabilityKind::parse accepts canonical Process/Group tokens (bn-2l3n)"}	blake3:w2cAxDQf3-FDlmoPY0GRqm5sE-Q-_cy2_dXOnEaWQBM
1784839637073403	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExpxA		item.move	bn-354w	{"state":"done"}	blake3:T7QiPnMiqFdUPkkrXbi_P5Lv_kKHgbYO1U-cJ2uDV8I
1784845183170499	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExqBA		item.create	bn-2gus	{"description":"The rehearsal fail-stops with 'current-child children execution tools dev-null live identity differs' (exit 2) whenever /dev's directory ctime/mtime changes between build-children and the rehearsal. /dev is devtmpfs: its timestamps bump on ANY device add/remove, which happens routinely while the machine is in use during the ~1.5h build. _semantic_null_device and _semantic_current_tool compare the full recorded parent/path chain (including changed_ns/modified_ns/size/link_count) against a live recompute, so a volatile parent-dir timestamp fail-stops the whole run. This is the same fragility bn-1csq fixed for _semantic_directory_identity (dropped nlink/size/mtime/ctime for ancestor dirs). Fix: compare chains on structural anti-swap identity only (device, inode, mode, uid, gid, type, path); the /dev/null node identity and file sha256 pins remain strict. Directly addresses 'preventing normal use of my machine' during builds.","kind":"task","title":"fix: tolerate volatile parent-dir timestamps in dev-null/tool path chains (bn-2l3n)"}	blake3:cvnB8pxPjBXD9dAlIRIqWJ71Uzceax6GJYVQbj7a8yE
1784845385799709	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExqRA		item.move	bn-2gus	{"state":"done"}	blake3:xbgavnnsDdRWGwenPJrpCTuhFEm1U2JFPtfQUmxQgI0
1784850966933518	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExqhA		item.create	bn-3f7n	{"description":"profile_adapters._rich_result:3992 requires start_sent <= release_monotonic <= t0 for non-reopen cells, but the child (bare/public main.rs) records t0 (line 278/414) BEFORE release_monotonic (line 279/415), and the canonical evidence_schema (7797-7807) validates the phase markers monotone as ...t0 <= release_monotonic <= last_completion <= t1... So the check has release and t0 swapped -> ProfileEvidenceError('control start/release/t0 ordering differs') at the primary-post guard the first time a primary measurement cell completes. Never caught: only non-reopen primary cells hit 3992 and no rehearsal reached them until v18. Fix: t0 <= release_monotonic <= last_completion, matching evidence_schema and the child. Big lifecycle check, reopen branch, and perf enable/disable ordering all verified correct.","kind":"task","title":"fix: correct inverted release/t0 ordering in profile control lifecycle (bn-2l3n)"}	blake3:eXjsgspxTInCWpfWQ2y0cZQwV_hi8W3FdA7-2qJakDE
1784851263447621	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExqxA		item.move	bn-3f7n	{"state":"done"}	blake3:H3J7QgjPez8wf6dJiSmjlz35rcL0djtMGWEQS7VS5lQ
1784853248803681	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExrBA		item.create	bn-2twx	{"description":"Audit found 8 divergences in profile_adapters trace/perf parsing vs the real perf/strace producers (empirically verified: perf emits 7 CSV fields not 5-6; strace writes JSON then LF as separate writes; strace -yy socket annotation contains '->'; -f splits blocked futex into unfinished/resumed across interval edges; SIGSTOP parking emits '--- SIG ---' frames; interleaved fsync renders unfinished; directory fsync; 16MiB cap). Each fail-stops cpu_profiles/syscall_profiles/structural_traces cells. Fix the parsers to match real output; update the stubbed test fixtures that encode fake producer behavior.","kind":"task","title":"fix: profile_adapters perf/strace trace parsers match real producer output (bn-2l3n)"}	blake3:FNTCW8bzci498WIWZLOC1GLNzadPJEATXy1pPUapdyE
1784854497305022	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExrRA		item.move	bn-2twx	{"state":"done"}	blake3:08MyOUlWwugi0kuP2TmuFdSQsdFHO5OY6vGTtCSBnOc
1784860381708726	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExrhA		item.create	bn-1roy	{"description":"profile_adapters._primary_profile_fields (3473) and the cpu_profiles branch (4249) call require_measurable_role_cpu, which HARD-FAILS (ProfileEvidenceError) when the critical role's on_cpu_ns is below the decision floor (20 x schedstat resolution). But the smallest/most I/O-bound cells legitimately have a critical role (owner) whose CPU is below floor (fsync wait is not CPU), and the canonical evaluator is EXPLICITLY designed to treat this as INCONCLUSIVE (evaluate.py:10780-10781 primary, 10714 cpu-profile-resolution). The runner's hard-fail dead-codes that path and fail-stops the rehearsal at the first primary cell (role CPU 11.7ms < 402ms floor), preventing the expected INCONCLUSIVE terminal outcome. evidence_schema does NOT enforce the floor (only records decision_floor_ns). Fix: remove the two runner-side require_measurable_role_cpu hard-fails; serialized_role_cpu_ns still recorded and the evaluator concludes INCONCLUSIVE.","kind":"task","title":"fix: below-floor critical-role CPU is INCONCLUSIVE, not a fail-stop (bn-2l3n)"}	blake3:U0iv38XQsQp20IMQ_VLoquYva_hQZ0SDrCqau4H0YpQ
1784860806111707	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExrxA		item.move	bn-1roy	{"state":"done"}	blake3:T6HMHDnH0uZGeZxSLaai6jQE0Zgao6jNqgYyIBan8iM
1784866089140928	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExsBA		item.create	bn-1qvr	{"description":"The producer-runtime role birth check fail-stops: 'role producer-runtime has unexpected births: [tokio-rt-worker x2]'. The harness pins the tokio worker thread comm as 'tokio-runtime-w' (old tokio default 'tokio-runtime-worker' truncated) in profile_adapters.TOKIO_WORKER_COMM, evidence_schema.PROFILE_TOKIO_WORKER_COMM, run_rebaseline self-test, and test fixtures. But tokio 1.48+ changed its DEFAULT worker thread name to 'tokio-rt-worker' (verified in tokio-1.50.0/src/runtime/builder.rs:291 and its doc 'The default name is tokio-rt-worker'; the overlay sets no .thread_name so it uses the default). Shared stale constant across the whole harness. Fix: update all 'tokio-runtime-w' -> 'tokio-rt-worker'.","kind":"task","title":"fix: tokio worker comm is tokio-rt-worker not tokio-runtime-w (bn-2l3n)"}	blake3:VAj4MBNRrAi1rTn1Ms17PEiYn8WYCcBTljOAuqzOhFc
1784866390240076	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExsRA		item.move	bn-1qvr	{"state":"done"}	blake3:y61RXX-w3yfCl0-vkj3PhVLyCGHZqex664HKHxaReKU
1784903006118184	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExshA		item.create	bn-1gle	{"description":"Variant C (writers=4) fail-stops non-deterministically: 'role producer-runtime has unexpected births: [comm=ast-rb-c]'. A newly-spawned tokio worker inherits the process comm (the executable name, e.g. ast-rb-c) and only renames itself to tokio-rt-worker once it runs (prctl PR_SET_NAME in-thread). The live ProfileCoordinator.bind_birth_group birth guard samples the thread list during boot->runtime and can catch a worker mid-rename. The allowlist only accepts tokio-rt-worker -> spurious fail-stop. Fix: add the executable comm to allowed_comms for the producer-runtime (boot->runtime) and spawn_blocking-publication (ready->measured) tokio-worker birth groups, tolerating the pre-rename state. The descriptive role_rules config (cross-checked with evidence_schema) is unchanged. Only bind_birth_group's runtime tolerance is relaxed.","kind":"task","title":"fix: tolerate tokio worker pre-rename comm in producer-runtime birth guard (bn-2l3n)"}	blake3:uFxiZpmsz5VxQaFCiODP-OWo56OWmFI5G-HfPM_BxAM
1784903690875707	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExsxA		item.move	bn-1gle	{"state":"done"}	blake3:Rl4gvcqSLd_ZJxjmY8QDn1Y8SlGVydb58To40XJ2D7s
1784913008898311	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExtBA		item.create	bn-3mbj	{"description":"The full matrix retains every cell store under attempts/<nonce>/stores/; v23 reached 140GB across 429 rows before the 128GiB free floor. Since more disk is not available, reclaim space per row: a completed fresh measurement-row store is never reopened (store id is a name, not a content hash; require_store_after is a per-cell check; no end-of-run pass reads stores). run_child reclaims each fresh measurement-row store (primary/cpu_profiles/syscall_profiles/new_names/fairness, store_absent_before True, kind not correctness/fault) once its evidence row is recorded. correctness/fault stores and shared corpora are retained.","kind":"task","title":"feat: reclaim completed measurement-row store space during full-matrix runs (bn-2l3n)"}	blake3:lVdWivTEi3Mi-P5JTkFR6u323fxvXYcH0J-bh3Ncyq4
1784913466854901	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExtRA		item.move	bn-3mbj	{"state":"done"}	blake3:Xyogdcvy4uUGEf-tY98lQZZc8OdWzK2bLTJ4PetnYAw
1784923949334714	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExthA		item.create	bn-3hd8	{"description":"At 68 min into the matrix (fairness track, variant B, 64 writers, Group durability), process_delta fail-stops: 'VmHWM rolled back within one process identity'. VmHWM (/proc/pid/status, mm->hiwater_rss) is a peak, but on recent kernels (host runs 7.1.4) it can be recomputed LOWER under heavy concurrent memory reclaim (64-writer memory churn), so after.vm_hwm_bytes < before.vm_hwm_bytes is NOT impossible. The identity (pid+start_ticks) is already verified equal, so this is kernel behavior, not PID reuse. Fix: keep the true peak as max(before, after) instead of rejecting the apparent rollback. Only kernel-sensitive counter in process_delta (io/context-switches are cumulative-monotone; cancelled_write_bytes already treated as signed).","kind":"task","title":"fix: VmHWM peak is not strictly monotonic under heavy reclaim; keep max (bn-2l3n)"}	blake3:g67Iu8BTs26TL1pCR9M00KstXBs-983LBx5KyYJe6Tw
1784924305742172	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExtxA		item.move	bn-3hd8	{"state":"done"}	blake3:BuPVDt2q1yFs8adyvVEA3URomxIVuYkCfiWmryvNqMk
1784929883102285	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExuBA		item.create	bn-n2lj	{"description":"The kill-partial-write fault smoke panics ~frequently (2/2 in v25; v24 got lucky): parent await_worker_ready (fault.rs:591) polls ready.is_file() then reads it, but write_ready_marker (504-512) create_new-opens the marker then write_all+sync separately, so the parent can observe the file created-but-empty and read '' -> 'fault worker marker differs left=\"\" right=case=kill-partial-write...'. Race between file creation and content write. Fix: worker writes marker to a temp file, fsyncs, then renames into place atomically, so the parent never observes a partial/empty marker. Child-side (fault.rs) -> build-children rebuild.","kind":"task","title":"fix: fault worker publishes ready marker atomically (bn-2l3n)"}	blake3:MYKyEhJKJ3yKzOk2N6EpZWqIviACYrsHFrCEKKx68xQ
1784929967264418	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExuRA		item.move	bn-n2lj	{"state":"done"}	blake3:9MBoVdgzkFL5DjHatDe0SbBg0CMH8ByQQy_G76b5O6Y
1784938980361499	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExuhA		item.create	bn-3qsa	{"description":"ProfileCoordinator.capture_phase enumerates /proc/<child>/task then stats each tid; under the fairness 64-writer cell a tokio blocking-pool worker is reaped between listdir and the per-tid read, raising 'cannot traverse proc path' -> child interrupted fail-stop at child 626. Same host-kernel-reality class as bn-3hd8 (VmHWM). Make ProcReader.tasks() retry for a clean pass and tolerate a reaped thread on the final pass rather than fail-stop.","kind":"task","title":"Tolerate tokio worker thread reap during /proc task enumeration (rebaseline profiling)"}	blake3:OXMB92961jypvVDHFn2kXcYvMXTM1LugjR0OPAPa4NA
1784939180010886	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExuxA		item.move	bn-3qsa	{"state":"done"}	blake3:uU6vLtcilTsA8knCd5T9qJm3vdECeY1fkZnxwmJsyCY
1784949961115580	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExvBA		item.create	bn-3nol	{"description":"First real syscall_profiles measurement cell (child 749) fail-stops: 'trace exact boundary/state invalid: begin=0 end=0'. The child emits ready/measured control markers via UnixStream::write_all, which Linux Rust std lowers to sendto(fd,...,MSG_NOSIGNAL,...), NOT write(). strace TRACE_SYSCALLS lacks sendto and the marker regex hardcodes write(, so markers are never captured -> begin/end=0. bn-2twx's write() assumption came from stubbed fixtures. Fix: add sendto to the 3 syscall lists (kept identical) and generalize the marker regex to accept sendto; update fixtures to real sendto form. Tooling-only; pinned child unchanged.","kind":"task","title":"Trace parser must recognize sendto control markers (Rust UnixStream)"}	blake3:B3wz1jq5b7hjPBguztDGF3bR37KdKU_NIa-a31dB7iM
1784950300068537	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExvRA		item.move	bn-3nol	{"state":"done"}	blake3:3MHg3GbHf-u2lCbnPjX-K3_ny_sPVYMmJxD5iy0SUVk
1784960353579288	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExvhA		item.create	bn-1pkm	{"description":"Variant-C fairness cells run warm_rounds=4 (public/main.rs:1320) which calls the injected spawn_blocking before ready; thread_keep_alive=3600s parks those threads so the in-window spawn_blocking reuses them -> zero ready->measured births -> bind_birth_group raises 'no phase births' (profile_adapters.py:1289). Flaky (v27 passed, v28 failed same cell). Legitimate ONLY for fairness (other C tracks warm_rounds=0 -> birth guaranteed). Fix: fairness-scoped allow_empty in bind_birth_group + end() call site + _roles empty-task guard; keep RoleDelta True flag and replay (empty==empty passes). Tooling-only.","kind":"task","title":"Tolerate zero spawn_blocking-publication births on fairness track (warm-pool reuse)"}	blake3:8M3kKI9LqlSsCfDbo0Ihv_5r8gMtWt-aibrapNFwwUI
1784960758030898	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExvxA		item.move	bn-1pkm	{"state":"done"}	blake3:ulrDDkCfUSG6uCd4F5qtPZLtnlKjJmxEmUSipftbc2Y
1784970720378823	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExwBA		item.create	bn-kyc6	{"description":"bn-3nol fixed begin marker recognition (sendto), but under variant B concurrency strace splits the measured/end marker sendto into '<unfinished ...>' + '<... sendto resumed>'. _TRACE_MARKER_WRITE requires a complete line ending in '= result', so the unfinished-form end marker is not matched -> begin=1 end=0 active=True fail-stop at child 750 (variant B syscall_profiles). v29 reached 750, past v27(749)/v28(642). Fix: accept the <unfinished ...> termination in the marker regex and tolerate result=None in _is_exact_trace_marker (count+fd+payload identify the boundary; interval closes at send start). Tooling-only.","kind":"task","title":"Trace marker parser must accept strace <unfinished ...> sendto markers"}	blake3:L_gWgM0c00DxA3a72WuZkyUCffaP_iJMiQ_g5_d0A24
