1785264137056272	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx0xA		item.comment	bn-2hza	{"body":"Re-landed on trunk @ e415b6d8. Verbatim restore of the engine.rs hunk from reverted commit 10a1768a (diff and post-image both byte-identical). Review cr-35s3vq approved on the basis that mess-security already approved this exact diff in cr-3podjz (and the identical logic as overlay hunks in cr-1nmggb). Full just test 981/981 pass. NOTE for anyone unshelving asterism: spikes/asterism_rebaseline/tooling/current/product-test-overlay.patch now duplicates this fix, and validate_product_test_overlay.py asserts trunk engine.rs == pinned variant-A engine — that assertion is now deliberately false. Drop the cohort-gate hunks from the overlay rather than reverting trunk again."}	blake3:LOYmk_vtqHAAPzehDiF1a66eUmqZaxHkAOE0rbAeuUg
1785264137073425	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx1BA		item.move	bn-2hza	{"state":"done"}	blake3:uMoaoYgUt3T1Q9ibeA0RaE_YQcl0lHgCTogCj0Yx0t0
1785264147214686	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx1RA		item.create	bn-squ2	{"description":"The @mention review-request hook (hk-04n) fires 'vessel spawn ... edict run responder', but the spawned responder resolves $AGENT as the SENDER (mess-dev) rather than the mentioned reviewer (mess-security). It therefore sees 'No unread messages in channel and no message ID provided' and exits immediately, so no review ever happens and 'rite wait -c mess --mentions' times out.\n\nReproduced 2026-07-28 on review cr-35s3vq (bn-2hza):\n  - vessel doctor: all checks pass; vessel list shows no agent after the hook fires\n  - 'edict run responder' with no env: 'error: RITE_CHANNEL not set (should be set by hook)'\n  - 'RITE_CHANNEL=mess edict run responder': 'Agent: mess-dev / No unread messages ... / Cleaning up'\n\nThe hook does pass RITE_MESSAGE_ID via --env-inherit, but the responder appears not to use it for identity resolution, and $AGENT in the spawned context is the parent's. Worked as recently as 7d ago (cr-1e7dil, cr-2y0x00 both got real mess-security reviews), so this is likely a regression.\n\nImpact: every review request now silently gets no reviewer; the lead has to notice the timeout and approve manually.","kind":"bug","labels":["tracking"],"title":"[tracking] edict responder auto-spawn resolves reviewer identity as the sender, exits without reviewing"}	blake3:nJi6UhMqqWce5Yqg56Q2AahrOKxErNLchfpsHo8riK0
1785264249706965	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx1hA		item.move	bn-1gn1	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:9Tnsu7Z64msCrwbhFulcnC4riNze3HZOxo7FXVjdFaw
