1785274322894455	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx4RA		item.comment	bn-5hcg	{"body":"Framing: see the FRAMING CORRECTION comment on parent bn-o5b (2026-07-28). This phase is a set of hypotheses, not a certification program. Default gate for each child change is `mess-bench run --mode full --floors crates/mess-bench/floors.json` (~2 min, -10% per-metric ratchet) plus the ordinary `just test` / `just fmt-check` / seal review. Better or neutral -> keep; clearly worse -> drop or investigate. The batch-stratified matrices and ADMIT/DECLINE thresholds written into child Acceptance Criteria are context, not contracts."}	blake3:wcWe6Ixrkz3uR_Z2uSkrUYt-vp78WM8JnaVVftRLwvo
1785274322961256	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx4hA		item.comment	bn-3dos	{"body":"Framing: see the FRAMING CORRECTION comment on parent bn-o5b (2026-07-28). This phase is a set of hypotheses, not a certification program. Default gate for each child change is `mess-bench run --mode full --floors crates/mess-bench/floors.json` (~2 min, -10% per-metric ratchet) plus the ordinary `just test` / `just fmt-check` / seal review. Better or neutral -> keep; clearly worse -> drop or investigate. The batch-stratified matrices and ADMIT/DECLINE thresholds written into child Acceptance Criteria are context, not contracts."}	blake3:YgdUwgYBHkSRQNDvieEapB2Kgfv4zWMBnFf4MnsmEbo
1785274332791176	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx4xA		item.comment	bn-1cwy	{"body":"Reframed per bn-o5b FRAMING CORRECTION (2026-07-28). This bone is still a genuine keep-or-drop decision — that part stands. What changes is the evidence bar: `mess-bench run --mode full --floors` plus normal tests, judged as better/neutral/worse, NOT the matched stratified matrix with fixed ratio thresholds (>=1.25x apply, <=0.75x p99, <=0.7x memory, etc.) written in the Acceptance Criteria above. Those numbers came from spike reports and were never validated as resolvable on this host; bn-1gn1 demonstrated a 5% bar sits inside the measurement noise here. Decide on the direction and magnitude mess-bench actually shows, and say so plainly if it is too close to call."}	blake3:49zdSHo9zH5ZTb-i5qkfIG3ZiZ6a8zhrQ5hdX8UvfBo
