1785274346027236	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx6hA		item.comment	bn-37jh	{"body":"PUNTED per bn-o5b FRAMING CORRECTION (2026-07-28). This is end-of-project attestation — proving the finished engine to a distrusting reader — not iteration work, and it cannot produce a meaningful answer until the engine it certifies actually exists. It is the same class of work as the shelved bn-2l3n asterism rebaseline, which consumed over a week without ever reaching a terminal verdict.\n\nPunted so it stops surfacing in triage as if it were next. Not closed: if mess ever needs a published, defensible performance claim (a release, an external audit, a v4 default-on decision), this is the bone to reopen — and at that point the heavyweight protocol is the RIGHT tool, deliberately chosen. Until then, per-change regression is covered by mess-bench floors in CI."}	blake3:30gtyn81n_yl2ycZlw-_X0duZ19y-C5FYTsMO5qeq2I
