1785293252856826	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExiRE		item.comment	bn-34v8	{"body":"RESCOPED hypothesis-first (2026-07-28, Bob's call), per bn-o5b FRAMING CORRECTION.\n\nAs written this bone ends with \"No engine call site changes yet; integration is a separate bone\" — meaning it produces NOTHING MEASURABLE. It adds a mess-index component no engine call site uses, so mess-bench shows a flat line and we would not learn whether dense heads beat Book.heads until after paying for loom models, AtomicU128 capability selection, the seqlock fallback with identical semantics, and directory-growth hammering.\n\nThe hypothesis is \"dense heads beat the Arc<Mutex<Book>> head path\". Confirmed target: engine.rs:191 \"All engine clones share one Arc<Mutex<Book>>\", with heads: HashMap<u64,u64> (engine.rs:225) inside that mutex next to the registry and name arcs, so every head() read (engine.rs:364) contends with unrelated registry work.\n\nNEW SCOPE FOR THIS BONE — learn early, cheaply:\n1. Minimum viable dense head table, seqlock cells only. No AtomicU128 capability path.\n2. Wire it into the engine so it is actually exercised (shadow or direct), preserving semantics.\n3. mess-bench --mode full: does it move anything?\n4. Only then decide whether to buy the hardening.\n\nDEFERRED to bn-2yq5 (created for this), conditional on the hypothesis paying: lock-free AtomicU128 cells behind capability detection, loom models of read/write/grow, same-page and directory-growth threaded hammering, snapshot/export, explicit memory accounting.\n\nUnchanged and still required even in the minimal version: sparse/huge untrusted ids must not allocate unbounded directories (RegistryState density validated at the boundary). That is a correctness/DoS bound, not hardening, and does not wait on a measurement."}	blake3:8BYUBfvi7JT6Zkc69_1Qvis3_Flg4TfheZy-P7vEdAU
1785293263581229	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExihE		item.create	bn-2ig9	{"description":"CONDITIONAL on bn-34v8's measurement. Deferred from bn-34v8 when it was rescoped hypothesis-first (see its comment, 2026-07-28).\n\nOnly do this work if the minimal seqlock dense head table shows a real win over the Arc<Mutex<Book>> head path in mess-bench. If it does not, this bone closes unbuilt and Book.heads stays.\n\nScope when activated:\n- Packed AtomicU128 cells, used ONLY where genuinely lock-free, behind capability detection; seqlock fallback must share identical semantics.\n- Loom models of the real read/write/grow functions (not simplified stand-ins).\n- Threaded tests hammering same-page contention and directory growth.\n- Snapshot/export and recovery rebuild API.\n- Explicit memory accounting; Spike A's 16.02 bytes/stream target.\n\nSpike A reference numbers: 33-43M applies/s, orders-of-magnitude better concurrent reads than Fjall/RwLock HashMap. Treat as context, not a contract (bn-o5b FRAMING CORRECTION).","kind":"task","labels":["asterism","mess-index","state-kernel","roadmap"],"title":"Harden dense head pages if the hypothesis pays"}	blake3:0yuZIz03As4hE9160PZJUAT4U8z3D3cRjaYvSMYaeCE
1785293268143247	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExixE		item.comment	bn-34v8	{"body":"Correction: the deferred hardening bone is bn-2ig9, not bn-2yq5 (I cited an id before creating it)."}	blake3:mH5agjmjrheSJERXq4NEnHWDrQXzQtkPCWpnf4QzBpg
