1785542137282592	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExsRE		item.comment	bn-3hm4	{"body":"Lead verification and decision: DECLINE Phase 6. Verified the load-bearing claims independently: (1) publish_batch calls apply_committed once per batch with a single BatchEntry (engine.rs:1067) — Spike F's per-apply win is amortized ~1/batch_size in production; (2) ActiveIndex::resolve has zero callers in mess-store; (3) fold_chain floor failure the worker flagged is host conditions, not code — re-seeded under bn-40yp; (4) writer_retention 0.81 anomaly does not reproduce on clean trunk (measured 1.02, then 0.77 — the ratio bounces with host scheduling, which is why it is ungated). Max ActiveIndex share anywhere in the reference suite: 0.50%; best-case Amdahl gain +0.40%; predicted effect is 1-2 orders below the floors ratchet's resolution. The one double-digit share (reopen bulk apply, 18.6% of a ~31ms one-shot window in the degenerate 200k x 1-event shape) cannot justify four size-m risk:high bones. Workspace (instrumentation only) destroyed unmerged; snapshot recoverable. Coverage gap (no live-tail/global read workload exercises global_range/global_committed or hot multi-stream read_stream) filed as an independent measurement bone."}	blake3:eTiVI81jct5539jiwmnupczopBHS7rWZMzca3bAadXs
1785542137300948	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExshE		item.move	bn-3hm4	{"state":"done"}	blake3:rbwqPnNOTOQ2NSfzdl9WLG3ypTx7ptGwkeEG6uy6L0E
1785542148870734	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExsxE		item.comment	bn-1cwy	{"body":"DECLINE, recorded ahead of construction rather than after it (bn-3hm4 premise check, 2026-07-31). The gate this bone defines was designed to run AFTER bn-1fsu/bn-1yi7/bn-dxv0/bn-2c91 built the microblock stack; bn-3hm4 measured the bound on what that stack could deliver first: ActiveIndex is 0.0006-0.50% of composed-engine time across the reference suite (six of nine workloads never call it), because publish_batch applies once per BATCH — 2M events cost 401 applies. Best-case end-to-end gain from Spike F's 5.3x is +0.40%; the ratchet that would judge admission cannot resolve an effect that size. Component-level wins that batching has already amortized away cannot pay in the composed engine. Raw attribution tables on bn-3hm4 (two methods, counter instrumentation + perf, agreeing)."}	blake3:vg_wi8nT7nC73UK6qzPoHAHZM8CFXgyIi06utwPqKzk
